(6830818, 1026620, 20168, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the tribute Alexkc to my brown ribbon winner from July 11, 2008 <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=698076" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/889/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_698076.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/889/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_698076.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/889/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_698076.jpg"/></a>, a photo which scored 2.8289. <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=57229" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">raish</a> offered his own tribute to "Portrait of the Sky" with his <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=763201" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/990/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_763201.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/990/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_763201.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/990/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_763201.jpg"/></a>, for the "Brown Ribbon Deja Vu" challenge back in Feb ''09. Love the stars!</td>', 'Thanks for the tribute Alexkc to my brown ribbon winner from July 11, 2008 , a photo which scored 2.8289.  raish offered his own tribute to "Portrait of the Sky" with his , for the "Brown Ribbon Deja Vu" challenge back in Feb ''09. Love the stars!', '2012-07-30 16:19:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(6830850, 1026312, 108982, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neat:</b></div><hr/><i> Had potential, the crop is too tight, I don''t like that background at all, not very PRO like, seems over sharpened as well esp his eyes. Still having said that, cute kid, and I''m sure a lot better than the original </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I didn''t sharpen it at all it came from the lens that way, I chose to crop it this way because the young boy was shy and clung to his mom''s leg.  The background is her knit pants...it is what it is.  As for his eyes, they are incredible and that is their natural appearance.  That all being said, I appreciate your comments and perhaps will soften a portrait style shot like this in the future.</td>', 'Originally posted by Neat: Had potential, the crop is too tight, I don''t like that background at all, not very PRO like, seems over sharpened as well esp his eyes. Still having said that, cute kid, and I''m sure a lot better than the original   I didn''t sharpen it at all it came from the lens that way, I chose to crop it this way because the young boy was shy and clung to his mom''s leg.  The background is her knit pants...it is what it is.  As for his eyes, they are incredible and that is their natural appearance.  That all being said, I appreciate your comments and perhaps will soften a portrait style shot like this in the future.', '2012-07-30 17:03:04.000000', NULL, 0),
